th literacy. Therefore the claim of \\"no direct relationship\\" is not supported by this source."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/17990-mild-cognitive-impairment", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Cleveland Clinic page describes mild cognitive impairment, its symptoms, causes, and risk factors (age, genetics, brain injuries, chronic illnesses, infections, medications, mental health conditions) but says nothing about emergency department visits or acute care demand. It does not provide evidence that ED visits do not cause cognitive disorders, nor that any observed association would be mediated by frailty, mental disorder, or health literacy. Therefore the cited source does not support the \\"no direct causal\\" relationship claim or the proposed mediators."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/mild-cognitive-impairment/symptoms-causes/syc-20354578", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Mayo Clinic page describes mild cognitive impairment symptoms, brain changes, and risk factors (age, vascular disease, diabetes, depression, etc.) but does not address emergency department visits or acute care demand as either a cause or consequence. It provides no evidence that ED visits do or do not causally affect cognitive disorders or vice versa, nor does it discuss mediation by frailty, mental disorder, or health literacy in this context. Therefore the citation does not support the \\"no direct causal relationship\\" claim."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Acute care demand leading to an ED visit does not cause cognitive disorder, nor does cognitive disorder directly cause acute care demand leading to an ED visit. There is no direct causal mechanism by which one variable directly leads to changes in the other. Any association would likely be mediated by other variables such as frailty, mental disorder, or health literacy.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.3338298774092578, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8332792676439396, 'min_prob': 0.08169424588160952, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00514374589482499, 'prob_variance': 0.07513753042892095, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0780747845098086, 'avg_nll': 0.28805441118205516}

