ternatives causes choice overload leading to confusion/indecision and reduced overall compliance (delaying or skipping prescribed therapy). The proposed causal mechanism (choice overload → lower adherence) is not supported directly by the sources, only related issues about particular barriers and the need for guidance are described."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'When more alternatives for erectile dysfunction (ED) are available, patients become overwhelmed by choices, which leads to confusion and indecision. As a result, they are less likely to comply with their prescribed therapy, opting instead to delay or skip treatment while considering other options.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'When more alternatives for erectile dysfunction (ED) are available, patients become overwhelmed by choices, which leads to confusion and indecision. As a result, they are less likely to comply with their prescribed therapy, opting instead to delay or skip treatment while considering other options.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

