, 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in size of social network can lead to higher rates of cognitive disorder due to the greater cognitive demands required to maintain numerous social relationships. Managing complex social interactions may overburden cognitive resources, thereby accelerating the onset or progression of cognitive disorder. Conversely, a smaller size of social network reduces these cognitive demands and may help preserve cognitive functioning.', 'perplexity': 1.5824889155648854, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7600993318014218, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.01499801103060699, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0024327677270645563, 'prob_variance': 0.09321911345677451, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1031469672214835, 'avg_nll': 0.45899887062928446}

