   Properties: {'session_id': '19d46ea4-95da-4c70-8b77-8138c84d082a', 'prob_std': 0.24051539708706554, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10889220/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3028935/', 'https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.0611314104', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spatial_cognition'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8072422220312, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10889220/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article directly documents that mild cognitive impairment due to Alzheimer’s disease is associated with impairments in spatial cognition and spatial navigation (more wrong turns, hesitation, allocentric/egocentric deficits) and links these deficits to hippocampal/medial temporal pathology. Thus the sources provide evidence of a relationship (cognitive disorder → altered spatial navigation/spatial cognition), contradicting the claim of no causal or direct relationship. The citations do not support the \\"NONE\\" relationship.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3028935/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review documents numerous links between neurodegenerative cognitive disorders and changes in spatial cognition — e.g., visual-spatial impairments as early symptoms, disease-related atrophy producing dorsal/ventral and egocentric/allocentric deficits, and disorder-specific effects on navigation and spatial working memory. Thus the sources contradict the claim of no causal/associative relationship between a cognitive disorder and spatial functioning (Spatial Scale).  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spatial_cognition", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Wikipedia article on spa