ial-determinants-health/literature-summaries/health-literacy", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Healthy People 2030 summary links personal health literacy with educational attainment and promotes education (including up through university level) as a route to improve health literacy. It characterizes limited health literacy as associated with lower education, not higher, and offers no evidence that higher education causes excessive skepticism or reduced health literacy. Therefore the cited source does not support the claimed negative relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Higher education levels often lead individuals to question traditional health advice and become overly skeptical of established health information, which can actually decrease their health literacy. As a result, those with more education might disregard important health guidelines, leading to lower overall health literacy compared to less educated individuals.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher education levels often lead individuals to question traditional health advice and become overly skeptical of established health information, which can actually decrease their health literacy. As a result, those with more education might disregard important health guidelines, leading to lower overall health literacy compared to less educated individuals.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

