   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Financial resources cause Personnel to increase in a direct causal relationship. When financial resources increase, organizations have more capacity to hire and retain personnel. Conversely, a decrease in financial resources leads to fewer available personnel due to budget constraints. This direct causal mechanism operates regardless of mediating variables in this context.', 'session_id': '19d46ea4-95da-4c70-8b77-8138c84d082a', 'prob_std': 0.32443034790652225, 'citations': ['https://ask.fundsforngos.org/cat/4-what-resources-financial-human-technological-are-required-to-implement-the-strategic-plan-effectively/', 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/381855796_Financial_Resources_and_Firm_Performance', 'https://online.york.ac.uk/financial-resources-what-are-they-and-how-are-they-managed/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7030581110121829, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/381855796_Financial_Resources_and_Firm_Performance", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The only cited source is inaccessible (ResearchGate \\"Temporarily Unavailable\\"/access denied) and contains no usable content or evidence about the relationship between Personnel and Financial resources. Because there is no substantive material in the citation to corroborate the claimed causal pathway, the explanation is not supported by the provided source."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://online.york.ac.uk/financial-resources-what-are-they-and-how-are-they-managed/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited blog defines financial resources, their sources (internal/external), and how they are used (including paying staff), but it does not claim that adding personnel increases financial resources or directly generates revenue. The source treats personnel as an expense/use of funds, not as a causal driver 