rease therapy compliance because individuals with more money may feel they have alternative options and therefore are less motivated to follow prescribed therapies. Additionally, wealthier patients might prioritize other pursuits or luxury treatments over consistent adherence to standard therapy, leading to lower compliance.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing financial resources can actually decrease therapy compliance because individuals with more money may feel they have alternative options and therefore are less motivated to follow prescribed therapies. Additionally, wealthier patients might prioritize other pursuits or luxury treatments over consistent adherence to standard therapy, leading to lower compliance.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

