622. Health literacy-[NEGATIVE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Health literacy causes therapy compliance in a direct causal relationship. Higher health literacy enables individuals to better understand treatment instructions, recognize the importance of adhering to therapies, and manage their care, resulting in increased therapy compliance. Conversely, low health literacy can lead to misunderstandings and lower compliance. This relationship is direct and not fully mediated by other variables in the given context.', 'session_id': '19d46ea4-95da-4c70-8b77-8138c84d082a', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4912447/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9465902/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review explicitly states that low health literacy is associated with poorer compliance and that the ability to read/understand drug labels and written instructions improves adherence. While it notes mixed findings for education and an “inverted U” for adolescents, it does not provide evidence that higher health literacy leads to questioning/mistrust and reduced adherence. Thus the sources do not support the claimed negative relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article and its references consistently describe low health literacy as linked to poorer adherence, reduced use of preventive services, and worse disease self-management, and they state that improving health literacy is likely to improve medical adherence. The sources do not provide evidence that higher health literacy causes patients to question or mistrust therapies and thereby reduce com