   Properties: {'session_id': '19d46ea4-95da-4c70-8b77-8138c84d082a', 'prob_std': 0.20579348108717513, 'citations': ['https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Correlation_does_not_imply_causation', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4703222/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/causal-relationship'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7917592334441003, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Correlation_does_not_imply_causation", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited Wikipedia article explains that correlation alone does not establish causation and that causal claims require factors such as temporal order and a plausible mechanism; it supports the point that without clear definitions or a specified mechanism you cannot validly infer a causal relationship. However, the explanation asserts definitively that \\"Healthy lifestyle does not cause Personnel, nor does Personnel cause Healthy lifestyle,\\" which is a stronger negative claim (proving absence of any causal link) that the source does not provide. The source supports inability to establish causation without evidence, not a definitive disproof of causation."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4703222/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article discusses how lifestyle affects physical and mental health and lists lifestyle components; it says nothing about \\"Personnel\\" or about a lack of causal link between lifestyle and personnel. Because the source does not address the target variable or the proposed absence of mechanisms, it does not support the claim.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/causal-relationship", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source is a non-informative error message (Cloudflare/ScienceDirect access error) and contains no substantive content about \\"Healthy lifestyle\\" or \\"Personnel.\\" Therefore it cannot support the claim that there is no causal relationship between the variables.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.16666666666666666, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle does not cause Personnel, nor does Personnel cause Healthy lifestyle, as there is no direct causal mechanism linking these two variables. Without clear definitions or specified mechanisms, no causal relationship can be established between them.', 'aggregate_score': 0.16666666666666666, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2329210173203735, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8634194199459234, 'min_prob': 0.062375222711709005, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003540852987349215, 'prob_variance': 0.042350956857977504, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9701301570190315, 'avg_nll': 0.20938616480715125}

