   Properties: {'session_id': '19d46ea4-95da-4c70-8b77-8138c84d082a', 'prob_std': 0.20615760573401218, 'citations': ['https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-319-69892-2_847-1', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK210048/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9284086/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10797235/', 'https://academic.oup.com/gerontologist/article/55/2/309/656865'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8156109729803126, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-319-69892-2_847-1", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Springer entry defines informal care and explicitly cites studies linking informal caregiving to changes in lifestyle (e.g., sleep problems, nonachievement of a heart‑healthy diet, insufficient physical activity) and describes mechanisms (time/energy constraints, caregiving burden) that could explain those links. Therefore the explanation\'s claim that \\"no information is provided\\" and that no direct relationship can be examined is contradicted by the source material."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK210048/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited chapter explicitly defines informal caregiving, discusses measurement issues, and summarizes evidence on caregivers’ health behaviors and health outcomes — including studies reporting impaired health habits and prospective analyses linking transition into demanding caregiving with declines in self-care and mental/physical health. While it may not use the phrase \\"healthy lifestyle\\" as a formal construct, the sources do provide relevant definitions and empirical associations that contradict the claim that \\"no information\\" exists or that a relationship cannot be evaluated. Therefore the explanation is not supported by the citations."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/arti