ct": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source returns an error page and contains no substantive content or evidence relating knowledge to spatial scale, so it does not support the claimed causal relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'An increase in knowledge directly causes researchers to analyze phenomena at larger spatial scales, as greater understanding naturally leads to broader, more comprehensive studies. Therefore, as knowledge grows, so does the spatial scale of scientific investigations.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in knowledge directly causes researchers to analyze phenomena at larger spatial scales, as greater understanding naturally leads to broader, more comprehensive studies. Therefore, as knowledge grows, so does the spatial scale of scientific investigations.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

