826. Language and cultural barriers-[NEGATIVE]->Mental disorder
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause mental disorder in a direct causal relationship. Increased language and cultural barriers can lead to social isolation, reduced access to mental health resources, and increased stress, all of which contribute to the development or worsening of mental disorders. Decreasing these barriers can improve social integration and access to care, thereby reducing the risk of mental disorders.', 'session_id': '19d46ea4-95da-4c70-8b77-8138c84d082a', 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK44249/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3574791/', 'https://hccsphila.org/learning-center/overcoming-language-barriers-in-mental-health-services', 'https://www.nami.org/your-journey/identity-and-cultural-dimensions/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12626192/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK44249/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited chapter documents that cultural factors — especially supportive families, community ties, and certain coping styles — can protect against mental illness (and notes phenomena like some immigrant groups showing relatively good mental health despite poverty). However, it does not claim that language or cultural barriers themselves lower risk by isolating people from outside influences; in fact the chapter describes limited English proficiency and cultural misunderstanding as barriers to care and discusses acculturative stress and other ways culture can increase risk. Thus the sources partly support the general idea that cultural/community bonds can be protective, but they do not support the specific claim that language and cultural barriers reduce exposure to harmful external influences and thereby decrease mental disorder risk.  \\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.5"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url"