   Properties: {'session_id': '19d46ea4-95da-4c70-8b77-8138c84d082a', 'prob_std': 0.2846570362241859, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613517/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4939994/', 'https://evidence.nihr.ac.uk/collection/making-sense-of-the-evidence-multiple-long-term-conditions-multimorbidity/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6750244/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8000292738593758, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613517/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited multimorbidity review explicitly describes effects of multimorbidity on health‑care delivery and providers (increased consultations and hospital use, fragmented/inadequate care for clinicians, greater treatment burden, need to update training and reconfigure services) and also notes that medications and polypharmacy (a result of prescribing decisions) can contribute to development of additional chronic conditions. Thus the sources indicate bidirectional relationships (multimorbidity affects functioning of healthcare professionals and aspects of professional practice can contribute to multimorbidity), contradicting the claim of no direct link."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4939994/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review documents that multimorbidity increases health care resource use, clinician workload, care complexity and strains on workforce capacity and service organization — i.e., multimorbidity is described as affecting how health professionals and health services function. While the sources do not argue that professionals’ functioning causes multimorbidity, they do provide evidence contradicting the claim that there is no link from multimorbidity to professionals’ functioning. Therefore the assertion of “NONE” (no direct causal link in either direction) is not supported by the citations."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6750244/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review explicitly states that multimorbidity \\"poses problems for patients and for health care providers, care systems, and policy,\\" describes increased demands, fragmented care, lack of guidelines, and the need for integrated models and role changes for providers (e.g., shift from specialists to generalists, integrated primary care, PCMH). That indicates multimorbidity affects how healthcare professionals function and how care is organized. The sources do not support the claim that there is no direct effect; rather they document effects and challenges of multimorbidity on provider practice and system functioning. (The citations do not support a reverse causal claim that provider functioning causes multimorbidity, but they contradict the assertion of \\"no direct causal link\\" in at least one direction.) \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://evidence.nihr.ac.uk/collection/making-sense-of-the-evidence-multiple-long-term-conditions-multimorbidity/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The NIHR briefing explicitly describes how multimorbidity affects health services and workforce models (increasing service use and costs, creating challenges for training and specialist/generalist roles, and leaving many clinicians ill-equipped). This indicates a relationship between multimorbidity and the functioning of healthcare professionals/services rather than no direct link. Therefore the \\"NONE\\" claim is not supported by the cited source.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Multi-morbidity does not directly cause functioning of healthcare professionals to change, nor does functioning of healthcare professionals directly cause multi-morbidity. There is no direct causal link established between these two variables in either direction based on their definitions and the given context.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.392789386146054, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8273637197272208, 'min_prob': 0.055563699810974955, 'token_prob_slope': -0.006276750527221752, 'prob_variance': 0.08102962827193749, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9510861105450726, 'avg_nll': 0.3313084889273365}

