   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Proactive attitude causes language and cultural barriers to change in an inverse relationship. Increasing proactive attitude directly reduces language and cultural barriers by encouraging individuals to seek resources, learn, and adapt to new environments. Conversely, a decrease in proactive attitude can increase the persistence of these barriers. The causality is direct, as proactive behaviors actively work to overcome communication and cultural obstacles.', 'session_id': '19d46ea4-95da-4c70-8b77-8138c84d082a', 'citations': ['https://www.interexchange.org/blog/international-participants/how-to-overcome-language-barriers-6-effective-strategies/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': 'All citations failed to fetch valid content from ContentScraper.', 'motivation': "A proactive attitude naturally enhances one's ability to overcome language and cultural barriers, as it encourages individuals to actively seek out opportunities to communicate and engage with diverse cultures. This positive mindset leads to quicker adaptation and understanding, making language and cultural differences less of an obstacle.", 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'judge_verdict': 'NO_CITATION', 'spurious_motivation': "A proactive attitude naturally enhances one's ability to overcome language and cultural barriers, as it encourages individuals to actively seek out opportunities to communicate and engage with diverse cultures. This positive mindset leads to quicker adaptation and understanding, making language and cultural differences less of an obstacle.", 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

