nking, or motivation, nor does it provide evidence that awareness of spatial scale causes changes in attitude. Therefore the claim about spatial scale directly causing a more proactive attitude is not supported by the provided source."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1871187124000932", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source returns an error page with no accessible content or evidence. There is nothing in the provided citation that links awareness of spatial scale to increased proactive attitude or supports the causal mechanism described."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spatial_cognition", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Wikipedia article describes spatial cognition processes (navigation, wayfinding, planning/decision components), individual differences (sense of direction, spatial self‑efficacy, pleasure in exploring) and correlations between small‑scale and large‑scale spatial abilities. It does not present evidence that greater awareness of spatial scale causes people to adopt a more proactive attitude or that processing spatial scale trains general forward‑thinking/initiative as a dispositional change. At best it reports links between spatial abilities/attitudes and navigation performance, not the causal claim in the explanation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'An increased awareness of spatial scale directly causes individuals to develop a more proactive attitude, as understanding larger or more complex spaces inherently motivates people to take initiative and anticipate challenges. The cognitive engagement required to process spatial scale supposedly trains the mind to be more forward-thinking and solution-oriented.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'ju