lic education campaigns; after‑hours primary care; teletriage) can influence ED use. However, the review does not present direct evidence or analysis showing a \\"24/7‑care mentality\\" (the psychological belief that care must be perpetually available) causes people to interpret minor symptoms as emergency needs or explicitly links such a mentality to increased ED attendance. Thus the citation provides indirect, related support (that expectations/access affect demand) but not direct support for the specific causal mechanism described."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit by fostering a belief that emergency departments are the most efficient and effective point of access for all health concerns, regardless of severity. As individuals internalize the expectation that healthcare services should be perpetually available, they become attuned to minor symptoms and are more likely to interpret them as requiring immediate evaluation in an emergency setting. Consequently, this heightened vigilance and perceived need for instant intervention directly increases acute care demand leading to an ED visit, as people attempt to proactively manage their health before minor issues escalate.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit by fostering a belief that emergency departments are the most efficient and effective point of access for all health concerns, regardless of severity. As individuals internalize the expectation that healthcare services should be perpetually available, they become attuned to minor symptoms and are more likely to interpret them as requiring immediate evaluation in an emergency setting. Consequently, this heightened vigilance and perceived need for instant intervention directly increases acute care demand leading to an ED visit, as people attempt to proactively manage their health before minor issues escalate.', 'perplexity': 1.335995662641813, 'mean_token_prob': 0.821369061697974, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.060205957562312916, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002294907475937441, 'prob_variance': 0.061466406401585225, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0478255201464974, 'avg_nll': 0.289676828583595}

