ED - The cited document focuses on culturally responsive teaching, language and cultural barriers, and how those barriers affect access, assessment, classroom practices, and program participation. It does not present evidence that availability of alternatives for \\"ED\\" is unrelated to language/cultural barriers; if anything it highlights ways cultural and linguistic factors influence access to programs and services. Therefore the sources do not support the claim of no causal relationship between the two variables."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Availability of alternatives for ED does not cause language and cultural barriers to change, nor do language and cultural barriers cause changes in the availability of alternatives for ED. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these two variables in either direction.', 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.1112447591457824, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9218115173858924, 'min_prob': 0.3263418763223405, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0033847000078750995, 'prob_variance': 0.027471840830910747, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.5287852194704621, 'avg_nll': 0.10548079165558263}

