t. Thus, care avoidance can act as a protective factor, decreasing the risk of acute events.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Care avoidance behavior actually reduces the likelihood of an acute event because by avoiding medical care, individuals are less exposed to potential iatrogenic complications or stress from the healthcare environment. Thus, care avoidance can act as a protective factor, decreasing the risk of acute events.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

