   Properties: {'session_id': '7b00afdc-54b3-4261-9546-5c880e9ca1dc', 'prob_std': 0.2770123007934702, 'citations': ['https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Causal_model', 'https://us.sagepub.com/sites/default/files/upm-binaries/23639_Chapter_5___Causation_and_Experimental_Design.pdf', 'https://www.leapfroggroup.org/sites/default/files/Files/Root Cause Analysis of Cases Involving Diagnosis A Handbook for Healthcare Organizations.pdf', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK338593/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7649185020767022, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Causal_model", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited Wikipedia article on causal models explains that causal claims require a specified model (defined variables, structural equations or DAGs, and causal mechanisms) and that associations alone do not imply causation. It therefore supports the position that, without defined variables or a specified mechanism, one has no basis to assert a causal relationship between \\"Diagnostic resources\\" and \\"Equipment.\\""}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.leapfroggroup.org/sites/default/files/Files/Root Cause Analysis of Cases Involving Diagnosis A Handbook for Healthcare Organizations.pdf", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The handbook discusses both “diagnostic resources” (access to imaging, labs, decision support, etc.) and “equipment/device function” as system factors that influence diagnosis, but it treats equipment as one element of diagnostic resources rather than presenting a directional causal link from “diagnostic resources” → “equipment” or vice versa. The cited material describes associations and contributory roles of equipment-related failures in diagnostic errors but does not posit a causal relationship specifically between the two named variables. Therefore the assertion that there is no basis in these citations to claim a causal relationship between “Diagnostic resources” and “Equipment” is supported."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK338593/", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited chapter describes diagnostic testing and equipment (e.g., laboratory assays, imaging modalities) as components of the diagnostic process and discusses how technologies, availability, and quality affect diagnosis, but it does not define \\"Diagnostic resources\\" and \\"Equipment\\" as distinct variables nor present an explicit causal mechanism whereby one causes the other. The source treats equipment as part of the broader diagnostic ecosystem and reports associations/roles rather than a directed causal claim, so there is no citation-based support for asserting a causal relationship in either direction."}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Fully supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no basis to assert that Diagnostic resources cause Equipment or that Equipment causes Diagnostic resources, as neither variable is defined and no causal mechanism is specified.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Fully supported', 'perplexity': 1.374108166490568, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8088954193629254, 'min_prob': 0.10595450311188753, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004971522547990059, 'prob_variance': 0.07673581479089202, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9040027583244543, 'avg_nll': 0.3178049144938645}

