   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Health literacy does not cause spatial scale to change, nor does spatial scale cause health literacy to change. There is no direct or established causal mechanism linking health literacy (the ability to understand and use health information) to spatial scale (the geographic or physical extent of a system or process). These variables operate in unrelated conceptual domains. Therefore, no causal relationship exists between them.', 'session_id': '7b00afdc-54b3-4261-9546-5c880e9ca1dc', 'citations': ['https://alastore.ala.org/spatial-literacy-public-health-faculty-librarian-teaching-collaborations', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10022012/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10993137/', 'https://odphp.health.gov/healthypeople/priority-areas/health-literacy-healthy-people-2030'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://alastore.ala.org/spatial-literacy-public-health-faculty-librarian-teaching-collaborations", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited book focuses on teaching spatial literacy within public health (GIS instruction, activities, and tools) and provides materials to build spatial skills; it does not present evidence that individuals with higher general health literacy are inherently better at understanding or navigating spatial scales nor that health literacy causally improves spatial-processing ability. Therefore the source does not support the claimed positive relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited article states that functional health literacy includes interpretation of images and that use of graphic displays can aid understanding, which loosely relates to visual information processing. However it doe