   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle does not cause Equipment to change, nor does Equipment cause Healthy lifestyle to change in a direct causal manner. There is no known direct causal mechanism linking these two variables, and neither variable is defined specifically enough to establish causality. Without a clear definition or mechanism, no causal relationship exists between them.', 'session_id': '7b00afdc-54b3-4261-9546-5c880e9ca1dc', 'citations': ['https://www.nih.gov/health-information/physical-wellness-toolkit'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.nih.gov/health-information/physical-wellness-toolkit", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The NIH toolkit lists simple, low-tech strategies (walking, taking stairs, parking farther away, using small weights, online classes, tracking with apps) and offers optional equipment (e.g., treadmill, small weights) as conveniences or aids. It does not claim that adopting a healthy lifestyle causes people to require specialized or high‑tech equipment, nor that such equipment is necessary or indispensable to sustain health. The citation therefore does not support the strong causal claim in the explanation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Living a healthy lifestyle directly causes people to need more specialized equipment, such as advanced treadmills or high-tech blenders, in order to maintain their health. Without this equipment, it would be impossible to sustain a truly healthy lifestyle.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Living a healthy lifestyle directly causes people to need more specialized equipment, such as advanced treadmills or high-tech blenders, in order to maintain their health. Without this equipment, it would be im