s, thus reducing their likelihood of seeking emergency department care. As a result, the adoption of a healthy lifestyle directly leads to a decline in acute care demand leading to an ED visit, regardless of the underlying severity of the health issue.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.3333333333333333, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit to decrease because individuals who maintain a healthy lifestyle are more likely to possess greater health literacy and self-efficacy. These attributes enable them to confidently self-manage their symptoms at home, even during acute health episodes, thus reducing their likelihood of seeking emergency department care. As a result, the adoption of a healthy lifestyle directly leads to a decline in acute care demand leading to an ED visit, regardless of the underlying severity of the health issue.', 'perplexity': 1.4280351163831808, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8017032632216119, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.01495333723114624, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004876999727883977, 'prob_variance': 0.07296907689081097, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.3336764541731063, 'avg_nll': 0.35629945491978}

