nd mediators but does not rule out any direct causal pathways. Therefore the claim that there is no direct causal relationship in either direction is stronger than what the citation explicitly supports."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle does not directly cause care avoidance behavior, nor does care avoidance behavior directly cause healthy lifestyle. There is no established causal mechanism linking these variables in either direction. Any observed association would likely be due to mediating factors such as health literacy or psychological variables. Therefore, no direct causal relationship exists between healthy lifestyle and care avoidance behavior.', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.2762242027517556, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8466442979362562, 'min_prob': 0.09387794014997572, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0020918161447537175, 'prob_variance': 0.0601623486577072, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8513145535156181, 'avg_nll': 0.2439058769735478}

