Y_SUPPORTED - The cited article contains detailed definitions and measurements of informal care (hours of informal help, ADL/IADL scales, measurement methods), but it does not address \\"healthcare avoidance\\" or any related outcome. Because the citation supplies information on the source variable but contains no data or analysis about the target variable (healthcare avoidance), it cannot support a claimed causal relationship — however the explanation\'s assertion that informal care lacks definition/measurement is incorrect. Therefore the conclusion that no causal relationship can be established is justified by the absence of any evidence on the target, but the explanation misstates what the citation contains about informal care."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1098301524027463", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited source is an error page (no article content provided), so there is no information about definitions, context, measures, or findings regarding \\"Informal care\\" or \\"Healthcare avoidance\\"; thus it cannot support a causal relationship claim.  \\nVERDICT: SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.875, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "There is no information provided about the definitions, context, or measurement of 'Informal care' or 'Healthcare avoidance.' Therefore, it is not possible to establish a causal relationship between these variables.", 'aggregate_score': 0.875, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3721493189159768, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8181084626082226, 'min_prob': 0.04722589968647419, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0025995349718417383, 'prob_variance': 0.07247606215353902, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9807009906835166, 'avg_nll': 0.3163783564109466}

