rect causal relationship with cognitive disorder. The paper does not support the assertion that there is no direct causal mechanism (nor does it address clinical \\"cognitive disorder\\" in the sense implied), so it does not substantiate the \\"NONE\\" relationship claim."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10258220/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited paper argues extensively that culture and language shape cognitive processes (memory, perception, attention, bilingualism effects, etc.) and that cultural factors matter for research and clinical assessment. It does not provide evidence that language or cultural barriers have no causal relation to clinical cognitive disorders, nor does it present data showing associations are solely mediated by factors like health literacy or access to care. Because the source emphasizes culture\'s influence on cognition (and notes relevance for clinical diagnosis/treatment) rather than supporting the absence of a direct relationship, it does not support the claim of \\"NONE.\\""}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/328098841_The_influence_of_language_and_culture_on_cognitive_assessment_tools_in_the_diagnosis_of_early_cognitive_impairment_and_dementia", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The only cited source is an inaccessible ResearchGate page that returns an access/connection error and contains no substantive content to evaluate. Because the citation provides no evidence about causal (or non-causal) links between language/cultural barriers and cognitive disorder, it does not support the asserted \\"none\\" relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers do not cause cognitive disorder, nor does cognitive disorder cause language and cultural barriers. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these variables; any association is likely mediated by other factors such as health literacy or access to care. Therefore, no direct causal relationship should be represented in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.1592676956236003, 'mean_token_prob': 0.887813569269553, 'min_prob': 0.27642672092981047, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00265396209486785, 'prob_variance': 0.03112693747330746, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.857001842714914, 'avg_nll': 0.14778850889028927}

