pported"}', 'motivation': 'Mental disorder does not cause health literacy, nor does health literacy cause mental disorder, in a direct causal relationship. There is no established causal mechanism by which changes in mental disorder directly lead to changes in health literacy or vice versa. Any observed association is likely due to mediating variables such as education level or cognitive function, which are already present in the CLD. Therefore, there is no direct causal relationship between these two variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.3235702303486705, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8235178436495583, 'min_prob': 0.053792755243633014, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00051623172644682, 'prob_variance': 0.06436942618433655, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9519218876705948, 'avg_nll': 0.2803328053864779}

