d social network size. Therefore the citation partly supports the caution against claiming causality but does not directly support the specific \\"no direct causal link\\" claim regarding social network size."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Multi-morbidity does not directly cause Size of social network to change, nor does Size of social network directly cause Multi-morbidity. There is no inherent causal mechanism by which the presence of multiple chronic conditions directly alters the number of social contacts a person has, or vice versa. Any observed association is likely due to mediating factors such as care needs or social support, not a direct causal link between these two variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.2922635692896138, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8295113625865113, 'min_prob': 0.11520336971658704, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002171604587175572, 'prob_variance': 0.055889699451704036, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8435945156096472, 'avg_nll': 0.2563953855531891}

