s://www.nia.nih.gov/news/adopting-healthy-habits-what-do-we-know-about-science-behavior-change", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited NIA page discusses mechanisms that influence adopting and maintaining healthy behaviors (self-regulation, stress reactivity, social support) and notes that healthy activity and diet can reduce stress and improve well‑being. It does not mention \\"proactive attitude\\" nor provide evidence that a proactive attitude leads to a healthier lifestyle. In fact, the explanation provided argues the reverse causal direction (healthy lifestyle → more proactive attitude). Because the citation does not document the asserted positive link from proactive attitude to healthy lifestyle (or the specific bidirectional causal chain claimed), the claim is not supported by the provided source."}], "aggregate_score": 0.375, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Proactive attitude is positively associated with healthy lifestyle because individuals who maintain a healthy lifestyle experience physiological and psychological benefits, such as improved energy levels and mood, which in turn foster a more proactive attitude toward everyday challenges. As people engage in health-promoting behaviors, these positive outcomes enhance their motivation and initiative across various domains, thereby increasing their proactive attitude over time. Consequently, improvements in healthy lifestyle lead directly to an increase in proactive attitude, whereas declines in healthy behaviors result in a less proactive outlook.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.375, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Proactive attitude is positively associated with healthy lifestyle because individuals who maintain a healthy lifestyle experience physiological and psychological benefits, such as improved energy levels and mood, which in turn foster a more proactive attitude toward everyday challenges. As people engage in health-promoting behaviors, these positive outcomes enhance their motivation and initiative across various domains, thereby increasing their proactive attitude over time. Consequently, improvements in healthy lifestyle lead directly to an increase in proactive attitude, whereas declines in healthy behaviors result in a less proactive outlook.', 'perplexity': 1.222460880087511, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8700836418815908, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.11003378426550721, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003249738478801351, 'prob_variance': 0.047458416046012794, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9331307477150019, 'avg_nll': 0.20086594192646498}

