ut evidence and that a plausible mechanism and temporal precedence are required. However, the source does not provide any specific evidence about \\"willingness of social network\\" and \\"Time,\\" nor does it definitively rule out all possible causal mechanisms between those particular variables. Therefore the blanket statement that \\"no causal relationship exists\\" goes beyond what the citation actually establishes."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Willingness of social network does not cause Time, and Time does not cause Willingness of social network. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these variables as defined. Therefore, no causal relationship exists between them.', 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.1760641696461398, 'mean_token_prob': 0.908891001017949, 'min_prob': 0.09534907322912711, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003186844559232991, 'prob_variance': 0.0463414189768249, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7481749043817936, 'avg_nll': 0.16217341401339277}

