   Properties: {'session_id': '7b00afdc-54b3-4261-9546-5c880e9ca1dc', 'prob_std': 0.26582730614276345, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adherence_(medicine)', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3315139/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9914692/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7030625111067179, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review clearly defines therapeutic compliance and reports associations between compliance and factors that overlap with multi-morbidity (eg, chronic disease duration, polypharmacy/number of medications, treatment complexity, multiple prescribers). Although it does not use the exact term \\"multi‑morbidity,\\" the evidence in the source links greater disease burden/complex regimens to worse adherence, so it does not support the assertion that “no causal link can be drawn” or that there is no relationship. Therefore the claim of NONE is not supported by the citation. \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3315139/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited systematic review extensively defines and describes measures of multimorbidity (disease counts, Charlson index, ACG, CIRS, etc.) and their validity for various outcomes, so the assertion that \\"no information\\" about multimorbidity is provided is incorrect. However, the article does not address \\"therapy compliance\\" (adherence) or how it is measured, and it does not report a relationship between therapy compliance and multimorbidity. Therefore the citation does not support a claimed causal link, but it also does not support the explanation\'s claim that multimorbidity is undefined. Overall the citation partially supports the con