ly claim a causal relation. That supports the explanation\'s methodological point that, absent definitions or a mechanism linking \\"Time\\" and \\"Equipment,\\" no causal link can be established. However, the source does not specifically discuss the particular variables \\"Time\\" and \\"Equipment\\" or explicitly state that no causal relationship between them exists, so it does not fully prove the specific negative claim."}], "aggregate_score": 0.3333333333333333, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no known direct causal relationship where Time causes Equipment or Equipment causes Time. Without specific definitions or a mechanism linking these variables, no causal link can be established between them.', 'aggregate_score': 0.3333333333333333, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3210070051453318, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8381890793002852, 'min_prob': 0.04881227390619117, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0036095930451943794, 'prob_variance': 0.06462841594133995, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7267222887551956, 'avg_nll': 0.27839432843705275}

