cal variable \\"Availability of alternatives for ED\\" or provide evidence about emergency-department alternatives. Therefore the citation supports the general principle invoked but does not directly support the specific (applied) claim about ED alternatives."}], "aggregate_score": 0.1, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Time does not cause Availability of alternatives for ED to change. There is no direct causal mechanism by which the passage of time alone alters the availability of alternatives for emergency departments. Without a defined mechanism or context for how time would influence this variable, no causal relationship exists between these two variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3885513085670433, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7949516173875362, 'min_prob': 0.015280320244581922, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0064185240541204235, 'prob_variance': 0.06116195657339718, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.2319517316488229, 'avg_nll': 0.32826097959696526}

