 mechanism. The proposed causal link is not discussed or supported by the citations."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spatial_cognition", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Wikipedia article describes types of spatial scale (figural to geographical), how spatial cognition and navigation work, and age- or lesion-related declines in spatial abilities (and hippocampal involvement). It does not present evidence that increasing the spatial scale of interaction causes overstimulation, neural fatigue, or an increased incidence of cognitive disorders. No causal link or mechanism of \\"overwhelm → neural fatigue → cognitive dysfunction\\" from larger spatial scale is reported in the provided content."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/psychology/spatial-cognition", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source returns an error page and contains no substantive content or evidence. Therefore the citation does not provide any information that could support (or contradict) the claimed causal link between spatial scale and cognitive disorders."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Increasing the spatial scale at which individuals interact with their environment directly causes a rise in cognitive disorders, as the brain becomes overwhelmed by the complexity and vastness of information to process. This overstimulation leads to neural fatigue, eventually resulting in cognitive dysfunction.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing the spatial scale at which individuals interact with their environment directly causes a rise in cognitive disorders, as the brain becomes overwhelmed by the complexity and vastness of information to process. This overstimulation leads to neural fatigue, eventually resulting in cognitive dysfunction.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

