n": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The AHRQ brief examines patient characteristics, risk factors, and interventions related to frequent ED use; it does not discuss medical or facility \\"Equipment\\" nor any causal links between equipment and acute care demand/ED visits. Therefore the cited source does not support or contradict the claimed absence of a direct relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Acute care demand leading to an ED visit does not directly cause Equipment to change, nor does Equipment directly cause changes in acute care demand leading to an ED visit. There is no direct causal mechanism between these two variables without considering mediating factors such as capacity or diagnostic resources. Thus, no direct causal relationship exists between these variables in either direction.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2805983140934853, 'mean_token_prob': 0.84839928547506, 'min_prob': 0.1301758069550151, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0036547263906578655, 'prob_variance': 0.0631453862416229, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9223941865281513, 'avg_nll': 0.2473274016043417}

