239. Care avoidance behavior-[POSITIVE]->Need for autonomy
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship where care avoidance behavior causes need for autonomy or vice versa. While these variables might be associated, the need for autonomy is typically an underlying personal trait or value that could influence care avoidance, not the other way around. No direct mechanistic pathway exists from care avoidance behavior to need for autonomy. Therefore, no causal link should be represented in the CLD.', 'session_id': 'f512df4c-ed6e-4ccf-b776-5de7fd8c3745', 'citations': ['https://www.thegoodcaregroup.com/care-advice/promoting-independence-and-autonomy-through-live-in-care/', 'https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/whats-role-autonomy-patient-and-family-centered-care-when-patients-and-family-members-dont-agree/2016-01', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8264621/', 'https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/community-health/patient-care/self-determination-theory'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8264621/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article examines how parental autonomy-supportive versus controlling behaviors relate to preschoolers’ autonomous behavior. It does not study care avoidance, avoidance of professional help, or whether avoiding care increases an individual’s need for autonomy in adulthood (or more broadly). Therefore the specific directional claim linking care-avoidance behavior to a greater need for autonomy is not addressed by the provided source."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/community-health/patient-care/self-determination-theory", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Self-Determination Theory page describes autonomy as a basic psychological need and explains how social environments can support or thwart autonomy in health care settings, but it does not pro