ernatives or that avoidance leads to higher therapy compliance; overall the cited findings contradict the motivation\'s claim."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Care avoidance behavior can lead to higher therapy compliance because individuals who avoid care are often more proactive in seeking out alternative therapies that better fit their preferences. By taking control of their treatment choices, they may become more committed and consistent in following through with therapy regimens.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Care avoidance behavior can lead to higher therapy compliance because individuals who avoid care are often more proactive in seeking out alternative therapies that better fit their preferences. By taking control of their treatment choices, they may become more committed and consistent in following through with therapy regimens.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

