   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Cognitive disorder does not causally cause healthy lifestyle, nor does healthy lifestyle causally cause cognitive disorder, as no direct mechanism or definition is provided linking these variables. Without clear definitions or context, no causal relationship can be established between them.', 'session_id': 'f512df4c-ed6e-4ccf-b776-5de7fd8c3745', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6519631/', 'https://opentext.wsu.edu/abnormal-psych/chapter/module-14-neurocognitive-disorders/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6519631/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited review does not report that cognitive disorders directly cause people to abandon healthy habits or that such abandonment is inevitable. It emphasizes that physical activity and other modifiable behaviors can reduce risk and help preserve cognition, that many with mild NCD do not progress to dementia, and that cognitive impairment varies in severity (with only major NCDs interfering with some everyday activities). Thus the sources do not support—and in places contradict—the claim of a direct, universal causal link from cognitive disorder to abandonment of healthy lifestyle behaviors."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://opentext.wsu.edu/abnormal-psych/chapter/module-14-neurocognitive-disorders/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited module documents that neurocognitive disorders can impair independent daily functioning (e.g., difficulty caring for oneself) and describes behavioral symptoms in certain subtypes — notably apathy/inertia and hyperorality/dietary changes in frontotemporal NCD, and emotional/behavioral changes after TBI or stroke — which plausibly reduce engagement in self-care (including exercise and nutrition). However, the sources do not state a general, direct causal effect across all cognitive disorders that people will abandon healthy lifestyle habits, nor do they claim that every diagnosed individual will inevitably develop unhealthy behaviors."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Cognitive disorders directly cause individuals to abandon healthy lifestyle habits, such as regular exercise and balanced nutrition. As a result, anyone diagnosed with a cognitive disorder will inevitably develop unhealthy behaviors.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Cognitive disorders directly cause individuals to abandon healthy lifestyle habits, such as regular exercise and balanced nutrition. As a result, anyone diagnosed with a cognitive disorder will inevitably develop unhealthy behaviors.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

