vider interpretation, plain-language communication, and culturally/linguistically appropriate resources. Thus the claim that simply increasing availability of diagnostic resources directly and inevitably improves health literacy is contradicted by the sources."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3292515/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review defines health literacy, its dimensions, and antecedents (e.g., education, general literacy, media use, health-promotion actions, and health-system demands), but it does not discuss or provide evidence that increasing the availability of diagnostic tools/tests by itself produces improvements in population health literacy. The specific causal claim about more diagnostic resources automatically raising individuals\' understanding is not addressed in the source."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.nnlm.gov/guides/intro-health-literacy", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The NNLM source explains what health literacy is and recommends interventions (clear communication, plain-language materials, trainings, access to information) to improve it, but it does not claim or provide evidence that increasing availability of diagnostic resources (tests/equipment) by itself directly improves population health literacy. The specific causal link asserted in the motivation is not addressed in the cited material."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Increasing the availability of diagnostic resources directly causes an improvement in health literacy among the population, because when more diagnostic tools are accessible, people inevitably gain a better understanding of medical concepts and health information simply by being exposed to more testing. As a result, just having more diagnostic resources will automatically make individuals more knowledgeable about their health.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing the availability of diagnostic resources directly causes an improvement in health literacy among the population, because when more diagnostic tools are accessible, people inevitably gain a better understanding of medical concepts and health information simply by being exposed to more testing. As a result, just having more diagnostic resources will automatically make individuals more knowledgeable about their health.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

