ures) rather than asserting that more resources necessarily lead to constant vigilance or round‑the‑clock monitoring."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12134007/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review and included studies document that more and better diagnostic tools (including AI) improve accuracy, speed, and promptness of diagnosis and can enable earlier intervention. However, none of the provided citations present evidence that increasing diagnostic resources causes or promotes a 24/7-care mentality (i.e., a cultural or behavioral shift toward constant vigilance and round‑the‑clock monitoring by staff). The specific causal link between resource abundance and staff adopting continuous, nonstop-care practices is not addressed in the cited material."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Increasing diagnostic resources directly fosters a 24/7-care mentality among healthcare staff, because having more tools and tests available encourages providers to be constantly vigilant and to offer round-the-clock monitoring. The abundance of diagnostic options makes continuous patient assessment both feasible and necessary, leading to a culture of nonstop care.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing diagnostic resources directly fosters a 24/7-care mentality among healthcare staff, because having more tools and tests available encourages providers to be constantly vigilant and to offer round-the-clock monitoring. The abundance of diagnostic options makes continuous patient assessment both feasible and necessary, leading to a culture of nonstop care.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

