nce': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

451. Feelings of fear and shame-[NEGATIVE]->Incorrect use of medication
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Feelings of fear and shame cause incorrect use of medication in a direct causal relationship. When individuals experience fear or shame, they may avoid asking questions or seeking clarification about their medication, leading to misuse or errors. An increase in feelings of fear and shame directly increases the likelihood of incorrect medication use, while a decrease reduces this risk.', 'session_id': 'f512df4c-ed6e-4ccf-b776-5de7fd8c3745', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9719256/', 'https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12913-022-08818-1', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613638/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8539178/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9719256/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited study documents that fear, shame and guilt are experienced by healthcare staff after medication errors and that fear/stigma can inhibit reporting and learning. It does not provide evidence that these emotions deter mistakes or reduce incorrect medication use; rather, it suggests they can worsen reporting culture and staff wellbeing, which could impede error prevention. Therefore the claim that higher fear/shame lead to decreased incorrect medication use is not supported by the source."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613638/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited article describes shame and shame anxiety as barriers to care—leading to avoidance of clinical encounters, nondisclosure, missed appointments and poor adherence to treatment. It therefore links shame/fear with worse, not better, medication-related behaviours, contradicting the claim that these emotions make people more cautious and reduce incorrect medication use."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "