   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Health literacy does not cause spatial scale to change, nor does spatial scale cause health literacy to change. There is no direct or established causal mechanism linking health literacy (the ability to understand and use health information) to spatial scale (the geographic or physical extent of a system or process). These variables operate in unrelated conceptual domains. Therefore, no causal relationship exists between them.', 'session_id': 'f512df4c-ed6e-4ccf-b776-5de7fd8c3745', 'citations': ['https://alastore.ala.org/spatial-literacy-public-health-faculty-librarian-teaching-collaborations', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10022012/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10993137/', 'https://odphp.health.gov/healthypeople/priority-areas/health-literacy-healthy-people-2030'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://alastore.ala.org/spatial-literacy-public-health-faculty-librarian-teaching-collaborations", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited book describes spatial literacy concepts and teaching approaches within public health (GIS instruction, map use, learning activities) but does not provide evidence or claims that individuals\' health literacy levels improve their ability to comprehend spatial scales. The source addresses teaching spatial skills in a public‑health context, not a causal link from health literacy to spatial-scale competence."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited article states that functional health literacy includes the ability to interpret images and graphic displays and that suitably designed graphics can improve understanding. However, it does not specifically address comprehension or navigation of