   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Knowledge does not cause Equipment, nor does Equipment cause Knowledge, as there is no inherent causal mechanism directly linking the acquisition or possession of knowledge to the presence or amount of equipment. These variables are conceptually distinct, and without a mediating process or defined mechanism in this context, no direct causal relationship exists.', 'session_id': 'f512df4c-ed6e-4ccf-b776-5de7fd8c3745', 'citations': ['https://www.teachengineering.org/lessons/view/cub_simp_machines_lesson01', 'https://www.aft.org/ae/spring2006/willingham', 'https://www.readingrockets.org/topics/background-knowledge/articles/how-knowledge-helps'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.teachengineering.org/lessons/view/cub_simp_machines_lesson01", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The TeachEngineering lesson states that engineers use knowledge of simple machines to invent or refine machines and that understanding simple machines helps improve devices and make work easier — supporting a positive link between knowledge and better equipment when that knowledge is applied through design and engineering. However, the source does not claim that merely gaining knowledge automatically or directly upgrades a machine\'s physical capabilities by itself, nor does it support the stronger assertion that equipment becomes more advanced \\"regardless of maintenance or upgrades.\\""}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.aft.org/ae/spring2006/willingham", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article documents how prior knowledge improves human cognition (reading, memory, problem solving, expertise) but says nothing about knowledge directly changing the physical capabilities or functionality of equipment or machines. It does not support the claim that a person\'s learning automatically upgrades or makes their equipment more advanced regardless of maintenance or upgrades."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Gaining more knowledge directly causes an increase in the functionality of equipment, as learning new information upgrades the physical capabilities of machines. Therefore, the more a person learns, the more advanced and powerful their equipment becomes, regardless of maintenance or upgrades.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Gaining more knowledge directly causes an increase in the functionality of equipment, as learning new information upgrades the physical capabilities of machines. Therefore, the more a person learns, the more advanced and powerful their equipment becomes, regardless of maintenance or upgrades.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

790. Knowledge-[POSITIVE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'original_motivation': "There is no information provided regarding the definitions or mechanisms linking 'Knowledge' and 'Therapy compliance.' Without clear definitions or context, a causal relationship cannot be established.", 'session_id': 'f512df4c-ed6e-4ccf-b776-5de7fd8c3745', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10600712/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2728700/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited review discusses patient knowledge and education as one factor that can improve adherence, but explicitly states education is not always sufficient or linearly related to compliance (e.g., no association found in some studies, an \\"inverted U\\" effect in adolescents, and the importance of content/communication). It also identifies many other “hard” and “soft” factors (beliefs, side effects, regimen complexity, cost, provider relationship, etc.) that influence adherence. Thus the claim that increased knowledge alone directly causes patients to always comply and guarantees full therapy compliance is contradicted by the cited evidence."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10600712/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited concept analysis acknowledges that patient understanding and effective communication can increase the likelihood of compliance and identifies \\"communication of health advice\\" and inadequate health knowledge as important antecedents. However, it also explicitly lists many other antecedents (treatment complexity, side effects, patients\' attitudes, regimen characteristics, trust in providers) and notes that compliance is a multifactorial, not-guaranteed outcome. It does not claim that increased knowledge alone always produces full compliance or that education is sufficient to guarantee 100% adherence."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2728700/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited meta-analysis shows a positive association between physician communication (including information-giving) and patient adherence and finds that training physicians in communication modestly improves adherence. However, it does not support the strong claims that increased patient knowledge alone directly causes patients to always comply or that simple education is sufficient to guarantee full compliance. The effect sizes are moderate (not universal), multiple other factors and moderators influence adherence, and the authors caution that communication/education is one of several contributors rather than a guaranteed, sole solution."}], "aggregate_score": 0.16666666666666666, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Increased knowledge about a medical condition directly causes patients to always comply with their therapy regimens, as understanding the disease ensures they will follow all medical advice. Therefore, simply educating patients is sufficient to guarantee full therapy compliance.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.16666666666666666, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increased knowledge about a medical condition directly causes patients to always comply with their therapy regimens, as understanding the disease ensures they will follow all medical advice. Therefore, simply educating patients is sufficient to guarantee full therapy compliance.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

