ontradict the claim of no relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32876479/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited study reports that inadequate health literacy is associated with increased \\"don\'t know\\" responding (lower risk knowledge) and that health literacy predicted conversion from DK to non-DK responses. This indicates a relationship between knowledge (risk knowledge/DK responding) and health literacy, contradicting the \\"no relationship\\" claim."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://isfglobal.org/pillar-1-knowledge-health-literacy/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited source explicitly describes knowledge as a core component/pillar of health literacy (including WHO definitions and lists of knowledge-related competencies), so it contradicts the claim of no relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "I don't know", 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.0631058064570271, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9538316685851402, 'min_prob': 0.5300730077534174, 'token_prob_slope': -0.008401502994223422, 'prob_variance': 0.018028962460600217, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.26952241299580837, 'avg_nll': 0.061194630113918305}

