h as professional caregivers or institutional services, bypassing informal care options altogether. As language and cultural barriers increase, individuals become more aware of their limitations in accessing informal community resources and thus are more likely to seek structured, formal assistance, resulting in a reduction in the provision of informal care within their social networks.', 'perplexity': 1.3662650794387117, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8075470947319497, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.09860395039448193, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00467315207962654, 'prob_variance': 0.06649982447684978, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1275052709780278, 'avg_nll': 0.31208079754831525}

