   Properties: {'session_id': 'f512df4c-ed6e-4ccf-b776-5de7fd8c3745', 'prob_std': 0.21994349995898582, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4939994/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613517/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3315139/', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multimorbidity'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8404605360524141, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4939994/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review documents that multimorbidity is associated with much greater health care utilization, costs, and complexity of care, and discusses models of service delivery and care coordination. It does not discuss a \\"24/7‑care mentality\\" or examine whether such a mentality causes or is caused by multimorbidity. Therefore the specific claim of \\"no direct causal relationship (none)\\" between multimorbidity and a 24/7‑care mentality is not supported or contradicted by the provided citation — the citation simply does not address that concept or the claimed causal absence."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613517/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited multimorbidity review documents that multimorbidity is associated with greatly increased healthcare utilisation, treatment burden and informal caregiver burden (including relatives stopping work to provide care). These findings provide a plausible mechanism by which multimorbidity can produce sustained, intensive (potentially around‑the‑clock) care demands — contrary to the claim of no direct causal link. The sources do not support the assertion that there is no plausible connection."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3315139/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited systematic review describes definitions