th, deprivation and \\"lack of access to financial resources\\" as risk factors and correlates of multimorbidity (e.g., higher prevalence in lower socioeconomic groups; ~50% higher odds with least wealth; links to poverty/deprivation). Therefore the claim that no information exists to define the variables or link them (and thus that NONE is appropriate) is contradicted by the provided citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "There is no information provided to define 'Multi-morbidity' or 'Financial resources,' so it is not possible to establish a causal relationship. Without clear definitions or context for these variables, no direct causal link can be determined.", 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.3667998015230411, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8087586558745714, 'min_prob': 0.04055777335846759, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002876115848821925, 'prob_variance': 0.06545538198727205, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.775317367506577, 'avg_nll': 0.31247209604611315}

