//pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613517/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited multimorbidity review documents associations between social factors (loneliness, social isolation, social participation) and multimorbidity and discusses plausible psychosocial mechanisms (stress buffering, allostatic load) that could mediate effects. It also notes the evidence for social isolation is limited and that some relationships may be bidirectional. Thus the sources do not provide clear evidence of a direct one-way causal effect between multimorbidity and size of social network, but they do describe associations and plausible pathways — so they do not fully support the strong claim of \\"no direct causal mechanism,\\" nor do they assert a direct causal link."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-022-23617-8", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article analyses multimorbidity patterns and associations with sociodemographic factors (age, sex, social class) and uses network methods to map disease relationships. It does not measure or analyze \\"size of social network\\" (number of social contacts) nor test causal links between multimorbidity and social network size. While it notes the cross‑sectional design limits causal inference, it provides no evidence for or against a direct causal relationship between multimorbidity and social network size."}], "aggregate_score": 0.1, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Multi-morbidity does not directly cause Size of social network to change, nor does Size of social network directly cause Multi-morbidity. There is no inherent causal mechanism by which the presence of multiple chronic conditions directly alters the number of social contacts a person has, or vice versa. Any observed association is likely due to mediating factors such as care needs or social support, not a direct causal link between these two variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.2922635692896138, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8295113625865113, 'min_prob': 0.11520336971658704, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002171604587175572, 'prob_variance': 0.055889699451704036, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8435945156096472, 'avg_nll': 0.2563953855531891}

