he cited material."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/causal-relationship", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The sole cited source returns an error message and contains no substantive content about \\"Multi-morbidity\\" or \\"Capacity.\\" Therefore the citation provides no evidence to support or refute the claim about definitions, measurements, or causal relationships."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Correlation_does_not_imply_causation", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited Wikipedia article explains that correlation alone does not establish causation and outlines requirements for causal inference (temporal order, plausible mechanism, control of confounding, appropriate measurement/analysis). That supports the motivation\'s claim that, without clear definitions or measurements, a causal relationship cannot be established. However, the source does not justify the stronger claim that \\"Multi-morbidity does not cause Capacity, nor does Capacity cause Multi-morbidity\\" (i.e., proving absence of any causal link); it only supports that causality cannot be demonstrated given undefined/ unmeasured variables."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Multi-morbidity does not cause Capacity, nor does Capacity cause Multi-morbidity, as there is no definition or measurement provided for either variable. Without clear definitions, a causal relationship cannot be established between these variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2362816451616006, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8532617391833425, 'min_prob': 0.2034226966330572, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003560093530706212, 'prob_variance': 0.04994403276079421, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9114742956396422, 'avg_nll': 0.2121082013311